@* Plan A17 (pass 26): the phasing side's vehicle movement: the vehicles that may spend MP now, read for the view (ruling R23.1), the chosen one, and its
   status, steps, towing, and Bounding Fire as the page renders them for it. The page keeps the choice and its reset rules. *@
<h4>Vehicle movement</h4>
<p class="muted" id="vehicle-help">
    A vehicle spends its MP one expenditure at a time, and the DEFENDER may fire or pass after each (D2.1, A8.1): Start for 1 MP, forward
    or in Reverse, or none when it begins in Motion (D2.12, D2.23, D2.4); a VCA change of one hexspine for 1 MP, 2 in woods, buildings,
    or rubble (D2.11); entering a hex its VCA points at, or in Reverse a rear hex at four or three times the cost, at the Terrain Chart
    cost of its movement type, woods for ALL its MP or, fully-tracked, half its MP, with a Bog DR (D2.2, B13.41, D8.2); VBM around a
    woods or building obstacle along a clear hexside for twice Open Ground (D2.3); a Minimum Move into a hex costing more than its
    allotment (D2.15); ESB for up to a quarter more MP at the risk of immobilization (D2.5); an OVR of an enemy-occupied Location for a
    quarter of its MP more (D7.1); and Stop for 1 MP (D2.13). It ends its move in Motion only when it cannot Stop or move on (D2.4); a
    bogged vehicle's first expenditure is its Bog Removal (D8.3). A vehicle waiting off board enters in Motion across its edge as its first
    MP expenditure, with a VCA holding the hex it enters, and the MPh does not end while it may (A2.52, D2.4; ruling R26.1). Stopped, it takes
    Passengers before it spends any MP, or lets them off for a quarter of its MP (D6.4, D6.5; ruling R26.2).
</p>
<div class="toolbar">
    <label>
        Vehicle
        <select id="vehicle-unit" value="@Selected" @onchange="@(args => OnSelect.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">choose</option>
            @foreach (var vehicle in Vehicles)
            {
                <option value="@vehicle.Value">@vehicle.Label</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>A vehicle that may spend MP now, and how it reads: its id and Location, or off board.</summary>
    public sealed record VehicleChoice(string Value, string Label);

    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<VehicleChoice> Vehicles { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Selected { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnSelect { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The chosen vehicle's status and actions.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
